  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Compound &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&#39; undergoes following sequence of reactions to give compound &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&#39;. The correct structure and chirality of compound &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&#39; is [where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Et</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>]</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8d19d13b-3959-418c-ae9c-02ca80e4f47e-image.png\" style=\"width: 251px; height: 70px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>Compound &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&#39;</p>",
