  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>In the first step the given alkyl halide that is 2-bromo-3-methyl butane reacts with Mg in presence of dry ether to form a grignard reagent,This grignard reagent reacts with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;to form a hydrocarbon (B)which has a&nbsp; chiral carbon.</p><p>In the reaction with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;grignard reagent behaves as a strong base.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/707bd95b-2ecd-4fe9-a95b-629827e5a6c2-24-08-2022.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 175px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
